# i.MX95 DPU topology, hand-written from the probe text of docs/imx95-probe-2026-11-28.txt
# (probe --raw output, captured 2026-11-28), at commit eab4162. Source: that file only.
# Written by hand, not by the converter. No hardware claim follows from cross-check
# results on this file: it is a recorded description, and a finding is about it.
#
# Constraints (scaling, source size, resource groups) come from profile imx95dpu
# (DriverProfile::Imx95Dpu), so this file has no scaling, max_source or group lines.
#
# Kept as recorded:
# - The probe lists two CRTCs; only the first (CRTC 39, the connected LVDS output)
#   is an output line. Plane masks are the probe outputs masks over that one output.
# - Plane 42 (primary) reports outputs 0b0: it belongs to the second CRTC (id 50,
#   inactive), which has no output line. Nothing can reach it from output 0.
# - Plane 31 is the only plane attached to the output at capture time.
# - zpos_now is the current zpos value of the raw dump for each plane. That is
#   Weston state at capture time, not a driver default: plane 31 has 5, plane 42
#   has 0, and the five overlays all have 1 (equal zpos).
# - Every plane lists 13 formats, all with modifier 0x0, in dump order.
# - The raw dump shows no rotation property, so transforms is -.
# - Blend modes are none, premultiplied, coverage.
xcheck 1
origin observed 2026-11-28 imx95-probe-2026-11-28.txt at commit eab4162
